1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,690
The story of Shaykh al-Islam Ibn Taymiyyah with a person afflicted by a jinn,

2
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:04,610
as told by his student Ibn al-Qayyim.

3
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:06,910
Ibn al-Qayyim says in Zad al-Ma‘ad:

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:11,090
I saw our Shaykh send someone to the afflicted person to address the spirit within him,

5
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:11,820
saying:

6
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:13,760
“The Shaykh says to you: Come out,

7
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:17,090
for this is not permitted to you.” — and the person would come to.

8
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:18,780
Sometimes he addressed it himself,

9
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:21,380
forbidding it from wrongdoing and reminding it of Allah.

10
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,230
This does not mean everyone who claims to speak with a jinn is truthful.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:32,060
Many charlatans exploit this, and ordinary people should not take on such a thing or expose the patient to harm.

12
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:41,480
Ibn al-Qayyim noted that harmful spirits most often overpower those whose religion is weak and whose heart and tongue are empty of dhikr, protective supplications and the Prophetic means of protection.

13
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,900
So protect yourself with the Qur’an and the adhkar,

14
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,150
and see a doctor if the symptoms persist.

15
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:49,720
Share this story with someone you love, and follow the channel.

